      "level": 2,
      "content": "A. Controlling Factors"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mass wasting is the downslope movement of weathered material driven by gravity without external transporting agents.",
        "Primary controlling factors include gravity, slope angle, water content, vegetation cover, rock structure, and seismic activity.",
        "Water content serves a lubrication effect that promotes movement on slopes.",
        "Hazards include loss of life, infrastructure damage, and blockage of rivers.",
        "Key mitigation strategies involve retaining walls, afforestation, drainage control, and hazard mapping."
      ],
      "id": "7weccwj"
    },
